# display-regs.list (item walleye-display-scanout-registers): the registers init-display-regs reads, one per line: NAME ADDRESS (read only, 32 bits).
# Bases (msm8998.dtsi, dpu_3_0_msm8998.h of Linux v7.3): mdss 0x0c900000; the DPU 0x0c901000; ctl_0..2 +0x1000/+0x1200/+0x1400; intf_1 (the DSI one, controller 0) +0x6a800; pingpong_0..3 +0x70000/+0x70800/+0x71000/+0x71800; dsi@c994000.
# Most live first: a read with a gated clock hangs the bus, the register before the hang is the last line the kernel log shows.
